      "message": "I am not sure \u0027del self[domain_id]\u0027 is correct for a multithread env.\nSuppose multiple threads call get_domain_driver for the same domain_id and they get in this elif. The first one will execute \u0027del self[domain_id]\u0027 succesfully, however the others will fail, since domain_id will be an inexistent key.\n\nMaybe we should change this to \u0027delattr(self, domain_id, None)\u0027, which should not fail if the key is not found.\n\n\n---\n\nAlso, we need a test case for this, in which i) the domain driver is loaded and we do get_domain_driver(domain_id) ii) its config is deleted and iii) trying get_domain_driver(domain_id) again returns None. Makes sense?",
